1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:10,525
Open a newspaper, and your eyes jump to the biggest headline, then the photo, then the small text. That order is visual hierarchy.

2
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:18,345
On every screen, ask: what is the one most important thing here? Make that the most visible.

3
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:29,800
On most screens there is one main action: buy, pay, or continue. Make it the most obvious button: filled colour, clear words.

4
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,850
Secondary actions like cancel or back are quieter: an outline or plain text.

5
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:44,650
CSS grid with auto-fill makes a grid that fits any screen, without a single media query.

6
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:55,925
Things that belong together sit together. A price close to its product name reads as one unit. Space is how people see groups.

7
00:00:56,620 --> 00:01:08,520
Use a few spacing sizes, like four, eight, sixteen, twenty-four and thirty-two pixels, the way builders use standard bricks. Then lay out your product cards.

